> Try $3500 (we like monitors and an acceptable amout of RAM), and no,
> not anymore.

You should shop around a little more.  A 533MHz 21164pc system with
a 17" monitor and 128MB of RAM can be had for around $2500.

As for "mass market," the 21164pc was *never* intended for the mass
market.  It runs DIGITAL UNIX, Linux, and Windows NT (and perhaps
some time soon OVMS).  None of these is a mass market OS, and DEC
certainly understands that. They never saw 21164pcs as being
a winner in the home pc market.

But many computer-savvy folks for whom floating-point performance is
important like the systems quite well.

