John DiMarco wrote:

> In any case, I don't expect this would be a problem that would be hard 
> to fix, since there are three perfectly good PCI slots in the Ultra 5, 
> and I don't see any reason why Sun can't support a 24-bit capable PCI 
> framebuffer in the Ultra 5, especially since they support plenty of 
> such framebuffers in Solaris x86.

But x86 machines have a BIOS in them already, and the PCI graphics cards
tend to have x86 firmware so they can be used by the BIOS at boot time.

If you had a PCI graphics adapter as your only head, you'd need it
supported in the Boot PROM.  Sun's don't (as yet) support a text-only
mode - even the Console boot screen is done by the pixel, which is why
it scrolls so slowly.  PCs do, and this text mode is pretty standard
between cards, so they work at startup.  But that doesn't help us here.

So each Sun supported PCI framebuffer would need Boot PROM support as
well as OS driver support...

I don't see an issue porting the x86 drivers for use as *second* heads. 
But I doubt Sun will be supporting a large number of different PCI
framebuffers for booting.  Unless they switch to using the text mode on
them?

