Hello --
Anyone with experience getting a 90TL to image load from a bootp server? 
There's almost no information in the Operator Manual other than that it's
possible.  I'm in the planning stages of converting serveral company remote
offices from bridged LAT to routed IP.  We're running OpenVMS 6.2 with UCX
on our main office server.  I'm used to MOP loading images on the company
LAN, but I will need some kind of a BootP server to handle this on a routed
subnet, correct?

Also, I have an application where, several times a year I set up a 56K
frame-relay link to a temporary location running 8 terminal servers but no
VMS server.  It takes forever to load the images over this miniscule link
from our main office.  Might it be practical to set up a Windows95 pc with
a bootp server to handle this?  As a test I setup "BOOTP Server95" from
Weird Solutions and enabled TCP/IP on a DECServer90TL, and it almost
worked.  The two devices made a connection, but the load timed out with
some kind of error.  I just don't know enough about what kind of parameters
the TL needs set up on the BootP server to make it work.

Any help or pointers to documentation would be appreciated.  Thanks in
advance.

