====================

I don't think things will change very rapidly, in the support ranks. 

Old platform support tends to depend upon access to people (hopefully
with the skills / experience) plus availability of sufficient
dependable spare stock to fill the kits and of course customers.  It
costs a lot in a nat'l or int'l company to maintain support for hw/sw
30 yrs old, and yes that cost gets pushed back to the customers
requesting such support.  It's not as simple a matter of "they have
the stuff why is it so expensive ?".  BUT ... DEC has tended to
provide support for anything they had the parts for as long as they
were able to do so with reasonable ability to repair.  Over time, the
kits get consolidated to areas where that product has highest density
and time to access the kits might increase.  That's sorta like life of
owning a classic vehicle.

I personally suspect it will take quite awhile for DEC  to change
differently than they have been changing over the past years in
regards to tech support.

of course ... all of these thoughts are my own and aren't worth the
paper it's printed on and I'll admit a pro-mother DEC bias from the
years when Ken would visit our site in his economy car (Pinto I
think).  I sorta wish I could go back to the time when DEC was family
and the PDP-11 was king.  Now it's just another  business.

