  I have a Storageworks raid array 310 (HSZ20) system, connected to
an AlphaStation 500 running VMS 7.1. HSOF software 3.1(?). There are a couple
of behaviors on it that don't seem quite right to me, I'm wondering if
anyone else who has one can verify these are expected:

  1.) If I insert or remove a drive ( which is not part of any current
storage units ), I get a message logged on the console port ( seems
reasonable) and then VMS report a mount verification failure for all
the units served by the controller, which lasts for about a second or so
and then resolves itself. Is it normal behaviour for all the drives being
served by the controller to report an error when an unused drive is added
or removed? This happens not only on drives resident on the SCSI bus affected
but to drives on the other SCSI bus as well.

  2.) The unit arrived configured for 2 internal SCSI buses - I reconfigured
it to handle a single internal bus and connected the second SCSI bus to
the external connector ( so I could add another drive tower ). I did this
by removing the terminator from halfway down the rack, inserting the jumper
in its place ( to jumper the upper shelf to the lower shelf ), and moved the
terminator to the bottom of the rack. I also changed the configuration switch
to "1" ( as documented in the manual ). This all seems to work except for one
problem - If I insert a drive into the bottom slot it comes up as unit number
2 rather than unit number 6 ( units 4 and 5 come up as expected though ).
Was there something else I needed to do to make the lower shelf use addresses 4,5
and 6 rather than 0, 1 and 2 ( it seems to be using 4, 5 and 2 ). I could probably
work around this by setting a hard coded ID of 6 on the storageworks brick, but
I'd like to know if the rogue id is a configuration or hardware problem.


   Any help on these issues, or other things to watch for on this gizmo, would
be appreciated.

