This is unproven at best. Alpha is generally perceived to be faster than Intel,it
is also generally perceived to be more expensive. Benchmarks that measure
performance and cost like TPC-C and TPC-D show that Intel has much better
price performance than Alpha when running NT.

What is even more embarrasing from Alpha terms is that the Intel boxes are
also faster than their Alpha competitors running NT, again using TPC-C and
TPC-D where performance and price are measured.

I have yet to see an industry standard  price performance server benchmark
that demonstrates that NT/Alpha has a performance or price advantage
over NT/intel Servers.

There are plenty of examples of desktop applications benchmarks like
PRO-E which show an NT/Alpha performance advantage but many of these
desktops are very price sensitive and Intel/NT seems to have the edge
currently in price terms.


