In article <Pine.SUN.3.93.980122185128.764B-100000@nansen.apl.washington.edu>, "Minh Cao H." <mcao@nansen.apl.washington.edu> writes:
:My window is lockup, key board and mouse not working.
:Would you tell me how to restart the window manager in OpenVms 6.1

  In general, the comp.os.vms newsgroup is a better spot for OpenVMS
  questions. 

  Two commands that are commonly used to restart the DECwindows window
  manager are:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:DECW$STARTUP RESTART
    $ @SYS$SYSTEM:SHUTDOWN

  The first command attempts to restart the window manager.  The second
  (obviously) restarts OpenVMS.

  I will assume you have access to the OpenVMS and DECwindows documentation,
  and can read up on the specific implications of these commands.  (And you
  may want to check with your site's computing services organization...)

  You will also want to indicate the platform -- VAX or Alpha, and the
  specific model -- and the version of DECwindows -- typically V1.2-3 or
  V1.2-4 -- and you will want to indicate if you have applied the available
  (and current) ECO kits for these DECwindows releases.  (You should have.)
  If the problem persists, you will want to indicate the particular graphics
  controller in use, and you may end up in contact with the local hardware
  support organization -- in order to verify the correct operation of the
  system and graphics controller...

