Digital has never understood that a LARGE segment of the market does not
consider price/performance in their buying decisions, and only look at 
price. Lets face it, you do not need a 1000mhz processor to do word
processing,
and running netscape. Had Digital had a VMS offering on alpha with entry
price the same (or at least in same ballpark) as Windows, it would have
made inroads into many more shops which, when they grow, will continue
to build on the scalable VMS instead of hitting roadblocks with Windows.
This also includes upgrade prices. The cost of the Digital software CD
is about $1000, right ?
This is before you get a licence/right to upgrade. UPgrading WIN95 is
about $100. So there is a long way to go before DEC can really compete
in today's world.

