Alpha and wait for IA64 which will become the only architecture left for
mass market.

If Compaq decides to push Alpha, the big winner will be Sun. Having 2
basic mass-market architectures (Alpha and IA64) will spur JAVA into the
lowest common denominator with software publishers going JAVA big time.
This will make it possible for other operating systems such as MACos,
VMS and UNIX survive based on
feature/costs values.



