Merced looks like x86++. No one who supports x86 has any choice but to
support Merced. If they don't support Merced, do you think they'll
support Pentium III? No, because there won't be one.

>10) Guess what happens next, given that Microsoft don't seem
>to like supporting more than one non x86 platform.


By the time we get here, your argument has faltered.

>>
>> >I still maintain that there is a practical difference between
needing
