Britt Jensen wrote:
> 
> Anybody thought about possible implications of VMS on x86 servers?

The 8086 platform is about dead and to be replaced by IA64 in a few
years. So the investment to back-pedal VMS down to the 8086 would
be a waste. Had DEC done this in early 90s, perhaps, but now, it is 
too late.

Whether VMS would be ported to IA64 I do not know anymore. Since Compaq
will have Alpha, perhaps it will be able to succeed where DEC was
either unable or unwilling to succeed : make Alpha popular.

As well, the logic to get VMS to 8086 was to be able to make VMS more
affordable by at least having a cheap platform. But with Compaq at 
the helm, perhaps it will be possible to have an affordable VMS which
runs on Alpha.

Furthermore, considering the design of 8086, I wonder what it would do
to VMS engineering costs in ensuring VMS is stable on that chip.



