While I agree, as usual, with Steve wholeheartedly, I have to add
something here.

Sun is aiming to compete on price with PCs to stop Sun low-end users
from moving over.  So they're not competing with what a PC has, they are
trying to provide a good Sun at PC prices.  And low end Sun users are
used to 8-bit framebuffers.  Gods, I only have 8 bit on my Ultra-1,
though I suppose that's low end now.  16 bit actually - I have 2 of
them. =O)

If you look at this as a cheap Sun, the decision to go 8-bit makes
sense, as long as you support 24-bit and fast 3D as an add-on.  Which
they do.  But most low-end Sun users don't care, and will be more than
happy with the speed hike at that price.

