On CNN's Business program at 19:00 EST tonight, (a short break from
CNN's live coverage of Clinton's bedroom), Both Compaq's president (I
guess I'll have to learn how to spell our favorite company's new true
head) and Bob Palmer were interviewed.

Palmer did not look comfortable. Maybe it was his first time on TV.


-Palmer said that the Compaq buys DEc was *HIS* idea which he got 
 YEARS (yes, an S) ago and relayed it to Compaq's president a long
 time ago.

-Palmer said that INITIALLY, Digital would operate as a wholly owned
 subsidiary. No mention of what would happen later nor of the definition
 of "INITIALLY".

There was no real discussion of Palmer's future. But Palmer did say
something to the order of "if it is felt that I can be helpful I will
gladly continue to work to complete the merger". My take is that his
future is either short term at Dec or has not yet been decided.

What is clear though is that his public admission that he has planned
this for many years, it has become clear that Palmer has worked to
sabotage Digital to make it possible for Compaq to buy DEC. It is too
late now, but frustrating to think that Digital could have survived had
Palmer not worked so hard to prevent Digital from growing.



