John J. Stafford wrote:
>    VMS' nitch is security, stability, maturity and excellent design.
>    It is Digital's responsibility to make that known to the people
>    who make the big decisions 'upstairs.'

January 2nd 2000, Big Corp's Boardroom in emergency meeting:

IT chief to Chairman:

	"At the time the decision was made to dump the expensive VMS
	 in favour of the popular NT, all the information given to us,
	 all the testing we did as well as all corporate directions made
	 by this company's board members resulted in NT being the only
	 choice and by far."

	"All software has bugs and it is impossible to test all of them".

	"Still, the few hours of downtime we experienced has cost the 
	 company much less than it would have cost to remain on VMS and
	 pay those exhorbitant costs". And if you look at the continuing 
	 dwindling of the VMS active user base, you will see that we made
	 the right decision as the software we need today is no longer
	 updated on VMS."

