I don't know if all Multias have SRM, but mine does at least (vx42).
Go to the "set up the system" menu (in ARC), and you should see
options for "switch to Digital Unix firmware".  Select, and reboot.
You will be in SRM.  You can get back to ARC just by typing "arc".

I have noticed that this seems to screw up my clock setting when I go
back to arc.  That might be a MILO thing though.  And, of course, you
cannot run NT from SRM...




