A quick look at the impact of the January 20, 1998 AlphaServer repricing
announcement reveals that Digital has eliminated the OpenVMS Price
Premium vis-a-vis Digital UNIX.

What's more, Bruce Claflin on January 21 sent a letter to the OpenVMS
installed base. In it, Big Bruce sez:

"I also hear your concern over our lack of support for OpenVMS in our
sales and marketing activities. 

We are making changes to fix this. Among them are: 

o Clearly positioning the importance of OpenVMS in our overall strategy. 

o Increased OpenVMS visibility in advertising, tradeshows, and public
relations activities. 

o Increased recruiting of ISV's support for OpenVMS in target markets. 
                          
o Pricing OpenVMS to remain competitive"

Complete details and an analysis of the repricing will of course be made
available to Shannon Knows DEC subscribers.

