Alpha PC's cost more than Intel - because not enough software is native (MS
Office etc) - because FX32 doesn't always work & is not officially
supported - because most games don't run. Now that the Intel/Digital
manufacturing agreement has been signed, Alpha is even more at risk; Once
Intel get the Alpha type architecture features incorported into IA64, what
