Subject: Re: Setting the VMS-display over a TCP/IP ISDN-router
Date: 1998/01/23
Message-ID: <34c8a97c.0@news.sto.telegate.se>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 319035505
References: <34c7a227.0@news.sto.telegate.se> <1998Jan22.132937.1@sldb4.slac.stanford.edu>
X-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V4.71.1712.3
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


I found it !!!

When setting up a display in VMS you don't have to give a number to the
/server.
But here I put the server == portnumber in the ISDN router. And it worked !

Client>telnet ISDN-router
ISDN-router>x enable command
ISDN-router>"Your display is aaa.bbb.ccc.ddd:portnumber"
ISDN-router>telnet VMS-host
...

$set disp/cre/node=aaa.bbb.ccc.ddd/tran=TCPIP/server=portnumber
$ mc decw$clock

A display !






