Hello everybody,

Our calculation to solve Certicom's ECC2-89 challenge is well under way.

The idea is to calculate a "discrete logarithm" in the group of points
on an elliptic curve.  There are 2^88+12377169451261 points which
means that we need to do about 25 trillion iterations of a
pseudo-random function until we find the same point in two different
ways, and then we can compute the final answer.

If you would like to soak up some spare Alpha cycles on this project,
then head over to:

  http://pauillac.inria.fr/~harley/ecdl3/


You just need to download a few K of source code, compile it and run
on Linux, Digital Unix or NetBSD (there are ReadMe and ReadMe.html
files with full details).  There are also some files with statistics
on our progress, which are updated every 10 minutes.

Currently 55 people are involved and we have done a little over six
trillion iterations so far.


See you there soon!
