Subject: DEC comes through, DEC C++ compiler vastly improved
Date: 1998/01/21
Message-ID: <6a5hv3$ioo$1@tesla.EECS.Berkeley.EDU>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 318084843
Organization: University of California, Berkeley
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec



I tried out DEC CXX 5.6, and found it to be very good.  Long ago,
I evaluated 5.1, didn't like it, and criticized it here.  Now I'm
happy with the compiler, and saying so!

Without trying too hard, I've gotten DEC CXX to compile binaries
which run significantly faster than g++2.8.0 or egcs-1.0:  
my programs run from 15% to 32% faster on my own benchmarks.

Furthermore, DEC CXX 5.6 compiles much more quickly than it did.
Compilation time is now comparable to what g++ achieves.

I did have to modify my code slightly from what worked with g++ to
get it to work with DEC CXX.  The changes were pretty minor, however,
DEC CXX wasn't difficult to port to, and every c++ compiler I've ever
used has had its quirks.  DEC's wasn't bad at all.

The improvement in DEC CXX is very significant.

The programmers who worked on it are to be commended!

Thanks to those who informed me of the vast improvement in DEC CXX
so that I would not miss out on a VERY good thing.

Peter Mardahl




