>CPU??  On the PC side, Compaq is where it is based on it's added value.

Of course on the U10 they added UPA.

As I have said in other related posts, Sun is a business and it
would be stupid business to put their best jewels in an Intel
box.  Especially when they can effectively compete with them
where they want to and cream them in other places.

>Since Sun owns the Solaris OS, they can tune the OS for their hardware
>be it Sparc or Intel. 

Solaris isn't bad on Intel now.  With the NCR & Intel agreements
it will only get better.

>But last, is Compaq, Dell and Gateway going to start selling Solaris x86
>based machines? No.  They don't now even though Solaris x86 is out.
