Are you implying that the reason Compaq, Dell, Gateway, HP, etc.
don't offer Solaris x86 is because either Sun won't sell it to
them or won't tune it for them?  I find that extremely hard to
believe.  They simply don't want to upset the giant that their
survival depends on.

So you think that Solaris is what should be pushed vs. NT?  And
that the way to do that is to sell Intel-based Solaris solutions?
I don't agree with that at all.  You see Sun is no different with
regard to Intel than Micro$oft is - you don't see M$ selling hardware
(well, at least not yet).  If M$ started selling systems you can bet
that their cozy relationship with Compaq/Dell/Gateway/HP would
go up in smoke very quickly.  If Sun sells the hardware then there
is NO chance that any of these other companies will be interested
in Solaris on their boxes.

And where does the Apple & clone comparison come from?  Sun
licenses many things to many clone vendors already - all SPARC
related.  I don't see the association at all.


