From: fdc@watsun.cc.columbia.edu (Frank da Cruz)
Subject: DEC and SGI <arpa/telnet.h> TELOPT_AUTHENTICATION
Date: 1998/01/22
Message-ID: <6a7pfu$ate$1@apakabar.cc.columbia.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 318342356
Organization: Columbia University
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.sys.sgi.misc


The DEC Ultrix, OSF/1, and Digital Unix (at least up to 4.0), and IRIX
(all versions, as far as I can tell) telnet.h files contain the following 
line:

#define	TELOPT_AUTHENTICATION 45 /* XXX Auto Authenticate */

But the Internet Assigned Number Authority has assigned 37 for this
purpose (RFC1416).  How can DEC and SGI operating systems engage in 
Telnet authentication with non-DEC and non-SGI systems when they don't
agree about which Telnet option is to be used?

- Frank



