Randy Rokosz wrote:
> 
> I'm trying to install WindowsNT Server 4.0 on a DEC AlphaServer 1000 4/266,
> which currently has Digital Unix 3.0-18 on its hard drive.
> 
> ------
> I tried putting in a CD marked "Microsoft Windows NT Server", turn the
> machine on and it displays:
> eb.....ea.e9.e8.e7.e6.e5.e4.e3.e2.e2.e0.
> Then comes to the console prompt:
> >>>
> 

You have the console variable OS_TYPE set to UNIX, to run NT this
variable needs to be set to... NT  !
Do >>> set os_type NT
then reset the system. It will come up in the AlphaBios (or ARC console
on older boxes) and you will need to work through the menu's.
Depending on which console flavour you have, you should be able to find
a menu entry somewhere to install NT from a CD...



