In article <6a29b9$18a@bgtnsc01.worldnet.att.net>, 
Kevin Landry <klandry@worldnet.att.net> writes:

> Does anyone have any experience using Printronix Line Printers with a
> DEC Alpha (OpenVMS 7.1).  I am experiencing problems with all of my
> Printronix Printers.

I am using a P-300 in the following configuration:

    AlphaServer 1000-A
    VMS v6.2-1H3
    Emulex P4000 Terminal Server
    9600,N,8,1
    XON/XOFF flow control

A second CPU (VAX 3400, VMS v6.2) also uses the same printer occasionally.

The only problem we have is a bug in the Emulex P4000 firmware.
IF:
  1) The last packet of a print file has been sent from the CPU to
     the server...
AND
  2) The printer sends an XOFF to the terminal server before this
     last packet is completely transmitted to the printer...
AND
  3) There is a second file queued to the same printer...

THEN the P4000 terminal server will lose the fact that it had
been XOFFed.   It will then start sending the next file to the
printer, causing buffer overflows and garbage printing.

Other than that, we have had no problems, either with the Alpha
(since July 1996) or the VAX (September 1989).

