The Starion 300i uses a motherboard design that will allow you to install up to a
133Mhz standard Pentium (not MMX or MMX OverDrive). If you do install a P133, you
will need to change the base frequency to 66Mhz and the clock jumpers to 2x. The
settings are in the User Guide, Appendix A, page 8. The settings are J21, J22 and
J27 all on.

No change to the regulator is necessary.

