The 900i as shipped with Windows for Work Groups supported CD Audio. It used the
CD drive to the Boca SE1440 and included applications for playing audio CDs. You
can check to see if the CD is capable of CD audio by inserting an audio CD and
connecting a set of headphones to the audio output on the front of the CD. If you
hear nusic, it should be OK. If the music is still not playing through the
speakers, you may need to replace the sound card (although I would not think that
this is the problem).

You do need to have the correct drivers loaded, but in Windows 95, the drivers are
part of Win95. Check in the Control Panel/Add/Remove Programs/Windows
Setup/Mulimedia to see if the CD Player is checked. If it is, try un-checking,
ckicking OK (this will uninstall it), then go back and re-install.

regards,

glen kelley
