In article <884946096.523028@terra.ultra.net.au>, phaedrus@mailhost.ultra.net.au writes:
:Can anyone help with the following . sometimes when my Vaxstation 3100
:starts to boot. it stops at the following line 
:%DTSS-I-SETTDF, DTSS set new time zone diff.  THEN
:%RUN-S-PROC_ID ident of created process is 00000050
: Its ALWAYS at the last line. 
:its gives no trouble for a few days then starts again. The only way to
:get the syatem going is to turn the power off and on again.
:can anyone comment ?

  Enable verification of the system startup, and determine exactly what
  command is hanging...

  Is this VAXstation 3100 system connected to a network?  (It would appear
  to be running a version of DECnet-Plus (DECnet OSI) and DECdtss.)

  One would expect to be running DECdtss only if:

    o hooked to a network...
    o in a network with DECdtss timeservers...
    o not running the NTP client...

  If you do not require DECdtss, use the following commands:

    $ run sys$system:ncl
    ncl> disable dtss
    ncl> delete dtss

  DECdtss may *not* be the thing that is hanging here, however...  Please
  enable verification in the SYSTARTUP_V5.COM or SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (which
  name depends on what version of VMS/OpenVMS you are running) via the
  SET VERIFY command, the f$verify lexical, or the STARTUP_P2 parameter.

