> didn't say.  Since they apparently did not put DU on a single machine...

Actually, the article you cited says that they did use Digital UNIX 
as central (file?) servers, and Linux as rendering boxes. The technical 
reasons for using Linux were flexibility (free source code for custom 
system tweaking) and support for third-party hardware. The biggest 
problems with Linux were untested (buggy) OS code, a weak NFS
implementation, 
and setup/configuration headaches. Still, even including the increased
engineering costs, they feel Linux significantly saved them money.

As always, the tool depends on the job you want to do. None is 
universal.

