In V4.0B and ealier you need to have the option CDFS in your
kernel config file

	options         CDFS

but in V4.0D and later you don't need to ever configure it
into the kernel because it will dynamically load it if you
haven't and mount the CDROM.  That way you don't use any
memory for the file system unless you need it.


Sean Davidson



