D. Sean Davidson <davidson@zk3.dec.com> wrote:
>The DEC Professional 380 has a micro 11/73 cpu (same as the
>big lab 11/70 systems).

Actually the 11/73 CPU isn't the same as the 11/70 (although it was
advertised as a replacement since the programming model and speed aren't
all that different), it's a single-board Q-bus processor while the 11/70
is a Unibus machine with the CPU spread over many boards.  Anyway the Pro
380 has the same CPU chip as the 11/73 but running at 10 MHz (vs. 15) and
with a totally different I/O architecture.

>The network connection should be a thick ethernet connector.

Note that the connector doesn't work unless you have an ethernet board
installed (DECNA I think?).

