I search USENEt too, mind you.  I've been looking for a smaller or
midsize SCSI drive, and even with exhaustive USENET searches, no
decent deals showed up.  I finally bought a perfect Quantum Lightning
365  365 meg SCSI-2 drive at a recent La Crosse, WI hamfest-type
computer sale for $20, and I was grateful to get it for half the price
I would have paid for it on USENET.  Without the rare sale though, I
would have had to get it from USENEt for twice that much.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Note the date on this one:  At the time, I sold a WD Caviar 420 for
$90 used, on ebay.  Remember, on ebay, the bidders set the price.
Four months later, 420s were still selling there, and on USENET, on a
regular basis for upwards of $85.  Occasionally, they could be found
cheaper, but it was the exception, not the rule.  I wasn't dealing
with any 540s at the time, but they were selling for more than the
420s were.

It was perhaps very bad judgement on the part of the seller, offering
all four as a package deal rather than selling them singly, but $350
for the four as a package deal wouldn't have been bad at all.

JT ought to admit to it, he would have been making a royal chump out
of the seller if the seller had been fool enough to sell those four
drives for the $210 JT says they were worth...

>Subject:      Re: FS (4) Western Digital 540 meg Hard Drives, $400
>From:         76657.3375@!CompuServe.COM (<--- Remove the "!")
