  Actually, the Wangtek 5525ES runs a poor third compared to the 5099 (first)
and the 5125/5150 (second). By the time the 5525 came out, 8mm Exabyte tapes
were common and the cost of media was making the 1/4" QIC (which would be
redundant exept that the floppytapes are also called QIC) format uneconomical.
Of course, the Wangtek FAD was even less popular...

> Thanks to Murphy's Law, one usually doesn't find out the problem
