"Stephen W. Hodge" <shodge@opus.freac.fsu.edu> writes:

> Does anyone know how to alter the # of lines that are "rescrollable"
> with the side scroll bars?  It seems like the default is like 200.  I
> would like 2000.  I know it has got to be a decterm setting somewhere.
> 
> I am using OSF 4.0 with CDE.  I don't see anything on the "clickable"
> icons.
> BTW, I am NOT a techno person, so please be specific as possible.

The terminal emulator used with CDE is dtterm. You may execute dtterm
with th option -sl 2000 or create a X resource for saveLines of 2000.
(This would be an entry of "Dtterm*saveLines: 2000", probably in the
~/.Xdefaults file.)

I it's your system, you can modify the defaults by editing the
/usr/dt/app-defaults/Dtterm file to include the line:
*saveLines: 2000

See "man dtterm" for more details if you need them. 
