In article <34BE3DC1.57B@iosat.com>, John Andrea  <jandrea@iosat.com> wrote:
>I'm looking for a tool which will position a tape at the end of the last
>file. Solaris supports an eom option for mt, but DEC Unix doesn't seem
>to have anything like that.

What version of DEC Unix are you running?  On the 4.0 system here on my
desk, "mt seod" will cause most modern SCSI tape drives to go to the end
of recorded data.  Most Unices will also happily do a "mt fsf 2000",
where 2000 is bigger than the number of files on tape (OK, on some NRZI
1/2" tape transports this will go past the end of tape!)  The "mt seod"
is preferred on serpentine devices like DLT's as it allows you to go straight
to the end without seeking back and forth till you hit the end.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



