Will the "DEC" (or Digital) name ever become an asset instead of a
liability ?
I get the distinct impression that DEC has, since Mr Palmer's arrival,
tried
very hard to hide its name from its products.

So, what's wrong with associating a product with "DEC" which has had, in
the past, an image of high quality/reliability ?

Microsoft certaintly has no problems with its name appearing on software
