11E23-FH (circa 1984ish) minus a few items but including about 500kg of
original documentation/manuals.

I have been given the option of getting this machine operational for
this years 2nd year Business Computing students to carry out their UNIX
module in the 3rd quarter of the year, to contribute towards one of my
projects in my Business Computing Diploma this year.

I have looked through some of the documentation in an attempt to
establish what I need to accomplish this.  I find that I am short a few
items and would like someone or two persons experienced in the support
of one of these dinosaurs to point me in the right direction and answer
a few questions as they arise.

The hope is to get it running with a number of terminals running from it
for students to log into.

What information would someone need about this system to be able to give
me an indication of it's capability? While it is heavy enough to make an
effective boat anchor for any medium sized leisure boat (after the
attachment of suitable hooky appendages) I am hoping it can be restored
to a semblance of its former self.

However the first problem is that there was no monitor supplied and
according to the documentation a special cable is required to attach a
monitor of some description.

Is this cable essential or can something be constructed at minimal cost
to enable the operation of a standard Wyse terminal? The poly has a
number of these available.

The unit only has a single SCSI hdd fitted with no disk or tape drive
however until I can view something on the machine I won't worry too hard
about not being able to put anything onto it.

Hoping to receive some positive feedback from suitably experienced
individuals.

