In article <34BE3DC1.57B@iosat.com> jandrea@iosat.com writes:
>I'm looking for a tool which will position a tape at the end of the last
>file. Solaris supports an eom option for mt, but DEC Unix doesn't seem
>to have anything like that.

It depends on your particular tape drive, but Digital Unix certainly
can do that. From my Digital Unix V4.0B systems "mt(1)" man page:

NAME
  mt - Magnetic tape manipulating program
	....
  seod
      Space to end of recorded data. Currently, this command is only sup-
      ported in the SCSI/CAM tape driver.  Not all SCSI tape drives support
      this functionality.

Just tried this with a Sony AIT drive in one of our tape robots and
sure enough it worked.

