That is the only memory you can put in a 3100/2100. They ax out at 24 megs,
an absolute minimum is 4 megs, since you must add the sims in pairs,
though of course 4 megs will be a bit low.. ;) 
8 megs will run okay, but not that fun, 12 or 16 is quite fine. 

>
>  The SCSI cable is round wire instead of ribbon cable. Is there any
>reason that a ribbon cable couldn't be used instead, allowing another
>drive to be stuffed in?

There is no real reason why you cannot replace the existing cable
with soehting else but it is not recomended to put more than 2
drives in there, since there is not very good ventilation and the power
supply is not made for giving out that uch power- especially at power-up.
Most of the ventilation draws through the lower half of the cabinet, 
and if you have two rz23's _and_ another drive it can get pretty toasty
in there.. 


as for an OS, NetBSD/pmax is great, and if you can find an older release
of ultrix with a license, thats cool too ;)
the NetBSD release is very well-done and rather mature now, in its
third version. 
get it fro ftp.netbsd.org in /pub/NetBSD/arch/pmax
(i think)

