From: perrot@lal.in2p3.fr (Bernard PERROT)
Subject: Celebris XL 5166 hardware bug !
Date: 1998/01/16
Message-ID: <slrn6bveah.ab.perrot@rama.lal.in2p3.fr>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 316626747
Reply-To: perrot@lal.in2p3.fr
Organization: LAL-Orsay
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Hello,

I just upgraded a Digital Celebris XL5166 (which had only one proc, but
upgradable in biprocessor) with a second Pentium 166 processor.

And just discover an hardware problem : the first processor run at 166Mhz,
and the second at 133Mhz ! There is no separate jumpers for the clock
setting, the same are for the both processors. There are two jumpers for the
core/bus ratio, and after some tests, I discovered than one of them is
always off for the second processor (so the second cpu can works at 1.5x or
2x bus speed, but never 2.5x or 3x, i.e. 100Mhz or 133Mhz, never 166Mhz and
200Mhz).

I tried with another CPU module from another CelebrisXL5166, with the same
problem ! So, it seems to be an hardware bug of the CPU module.

Does anybody know this problem ? Know a workaround ?

Thanks in advance.



