Which version of VMS?  as of V6 there is a command in SYSMAN that will
set sysgen parameter startup_p2 to certain values to accomplish what you
are looking for.

STARTUP

  SET

    OPTIONS

      Example


         SYSMAN> STARTUP SET
OPTIONS/VERIFY=FULL/OUTPUT=FILE/CHECKPOINTING

             This example requests startup logging with full
verification,
             output to SYS$SPECIFIC:[SYSEXE]STARTUP.LOG, and
checkpointing.


It sets startup_p2 in the current file as follows

SYSGEN>  SHO STARTUP
Parameter Name           Current    Default     Min.      Max.     Unit 
Dynamic
--------------           -------    -------    -------   -------   ---- 
-------
STARTUP_P1                  "    "    "    "    "    "     "zzzz"
Ascii       
STARTUP_P2                  "VDC "    "    "    "    "     "zzzz"
Ascii       
STARTUP_P3                  "    "    "    "    "    "     "zzzz"
Ascii       
STARTUP_P4                  "    "    "    "    "    "     "zzzz"
Ascii       
STARTUP_P5                  "    "    "    "    "    "     "zzzz"
Ascii       
STARTUP_P6                  "    "    "    "    "    "     "zzzz"
Ascii       
STARTUP_P7                  "    "    "    "    "    "     "zzzz"
Ascii       
STARTUP_P8                  "    "    "    "    "    "     "zzzz"
Ascii       
The catch 22 of this is it does not set anything in modparams.dat, but
you could accomplish the same task by addding the following line to
modparams.dat and running autogen

startup_p2 = "VDC"
