>> >1. How do you start Win3.1 in standard mode?

win /s

>> >2. IRQ (Interrupt request) settings , how many types are standard?

1 RESERVED
2 keyboard (also cascaded to IRQ 9)
3 Serial Port (Com Port 2 and 4) (Also Ethernet Cards , but NEVER KEEP it
here usally 10 works)
4 Serial Port (Com Port 1 and 3)
5 LPT 2 (and/or Sound Blaster, some modems allow this)
7 LPT 1 (and/or Sound Blaster, some modems allow this)
8 RESERVED
9 OPEN
10 OPEN
11 OPEN
12 OPEN
13 Personally don't recommend
14  Primary IDE Hard Drive Controller
15 Primary



>> >3. Name three types of memory used in DOS mode:

DOS Mode only uses convetional natively
EMS and XMS (Extended and Expanded respectively) can only be used with
Memory Managers
HIMEM.SYS and EMM386.EXE.

>> >4. Name three types of RAM used in DOS mode:

If you are referring to memory cards this question is moot.
Memory cards are at a hardware level and are managed by the BIOS
if the BIOS can use them so can DOS.


>> >5. What are the four main system files used in Win3.1?

Main Configuration Files:
    Progman.ini > Program Manager
    Win.ini > loads programs during windows startup (silently (if possible)
as apposed to startup group)
                    also fonts, extentions assigments.
    System.ini > drivers and 386 Enhanced feature setup
    other ini files that are usally not relevent







