In article <34bbfcd9.0@news.pacifier.com>,
Christian Brink, CNE <strat@pacifier.com> wrote:
>>> >2. IRQ (Interrupt request) settings , how many types are standard?
>
>1 RESERVED
>2 keyboard (also cascaded to IRQ 9)

Actually, in a standard PC IRQ0 is the 18.2 Hz clock and IRQ1 is the keyboard.
IRQ2 is used to cascade the slave 8259A but IRQ9 is connected to the backplane
pin that used to be IRQ2 (and the ROM BIOS provides a real mode ISR that chains
to the IRQ2 ISR so that non-AT-aware software will work), anyway there is no
particularly common use for IRQ2.

>8 RESERVED

IRQ8 is the 1024 Hz clock (from the Motorola RTC chip).

John Wilson
