X-Deja-AN: 315348766
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: University of Maryland, College Park
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Ok, everyone relax, I'm not trying to start a flame war. I've
just gotten some curious results and I'm wondering if anyone
else out there in computational land has seen similar behavior
with their code.  We have a number of 500MHz Alphas running
DU 4.0b.  Since we recently picked up a dual cpu 266 MHz PII,
I decided to run some benchmarks.  For my latest Monte Carlo
simulation code (Fortran) the Alpha is only 1.5 times as fast 
as a single 266 MHz Intel cpu (running Win NT).  This was somewhat
startling to me since our Alphas were about 3 times as fast as
the old 200MHz PPro.  Has anyone else seen similar behavior ?
Any explainations ?  From all the grumbling, I was under the 
impression that with the PII Intel was just treading water,
but this clearly isn't true from my results.  

Jeff



