The DEC VR 319 is a Monochrome monitor and is not really worth
trying to get it working as a PC compatible unit. The VR299 
monitors are "Fixed Frequency" units, set to power up at 54 kHz,
 also require a Sync-on-Green video input signal and can be used 
as a perfectly PC compatible unit, using a MIRAGE video card. 

For details on MIRAGE line of fixed frequency products, check
the following URLs:

http://www.mirage-mmc.com

http://www.mirage-mmc.com/dec/

If interested in finding-out about the Fixed Frequency monitors
and their differnce with MultiSync monitors, check the following
URL:

http://www.mirage-mmc.com/faq/

I do not know their exact market value, but if you need an
affordable solution to have a 20" screen on your desk,
they are as good as you want them to be.




