  To be used under OpenVMS, a CD-ROM drive has to be capable of 512 byte
  sector operations.  DIGITAL CD-ROM drives are capable of this, as are
  some drives from some other vendors -- however, many CD-ROM drives are
  designed (only) for 2048 byte sectors.

  OpenVMS V6.2 and later are much better about connecting to random SCSI
  widgets, but please remember that none of the S's in SCSI are STANDARD.
  Each SCSI device requires somebody to pay for and to perform integration
  and testing.  (And with DIGITAL drives, that has already occured.)

