"Minh H. Cao" <mhc1587@fennel.ca.boeing.com> wrote:

>
>Hi all,
>
>Would you help me to create a remote print queue on OpenVMS 6.2 .
>
>I used "multinet configure /printers" to create the remote printer.
>Do I need to run any command for starting the deamon, queue ?
>
from a system-level acount execute the command procedure
@MULTINET:REMOTE-PRINTER-QUEUES.COM

This will start any queues configured with the
MULTINET:CONFIGURE/PRINTERS utility.

>On the print server, what should I do to setup and activate 
>the queue for remote host ?
>

First of all, when configuring an LPD queue, the "Remote Queue Name"
is not an arbitrary name.  Rather it is a proprietary name assigned by
the manufacturer of the device (print server, jet-direct card, etc.)
and thus must be defined properly, for the appropriate print
functionality.  I will assume you are trying to set up a HP
Laserjet-5m here - most jet-direct style HP printers use a Remote
Queue Name of "Text" or "Raw" depending on whether you wish to do text
or postscript style printing, respectively (postscript is beyond me,
personally!)  Aside from that, the Jet-Direct manual is pretty good...
>
>Below is how my system setup:
>
>
>    HP-5m     Host-1                Host-2
>    Printer -- (print server) ----- (run "multinet configure /printers" )
>
>
>$ MULTINET CONFIGURE /PRINTERS
>MultiNet Remote Printer Configuration Utility 3.5(nnn)
>[Reading in configuration from MULTINET:REMOTE-PRINTER-QUEUES.COM]
>PRINTER-CONFIG>ADD laser5m
>[Adding new configuration entry for queue "laser5m"]
>Destination IP Address: 111.111.11.1
>Protocol Type: [LPD] LPD
>Remote Queue Name: [lp] laser5m
>[laser5m => 192.0.0.15, laser5m]
>PRINTER-CONFIG>
>
>
>
>Thanks in advance
>Minh
>
