In article <Pine.HPP.3.95.980109084030.27053G-100000@fennel.ca.boeing.com>, "Minh H. Cao" <mhc1587@fennel.ca.boeing.com> writes:
>Can you tell me what commands to show the
>printer's port number and TCP port number on OpenVMS ?

Depends on the TCP/IP software you use on OpenVMS.
And depends on which printer you had configured in the TCP/IP software.

eg. a HP JetDirect Card uses TCP Port 9100 (and 9101 and 9102) for Stream
and TCP Port 515 for LPD

UCX Stream:

$ SHOW QUEUE/FULL QUEUE
Printer queue queue idle, on node::"ipname:9100", mounted form POSTSCRIPT
  <Description>
  /AUTOSTART_ON=(node::"ipname:9100") /BASE_PRIORITY=3
  /DEFAULT=(FORM=POSTSCRIPT) Lowercase /OWNER=[grp,mem]
  /PROCESSOR=UCX$TELNETSYM /PROTECTION=(S:M,O:D,G:R,W:S) /SCHEDULE=(NOSIZE)


TCPware Stream:

$ SHOW QUEUE/FULL QUEUE
Server queue queue idle, on node1::, mounted form POSTSCRIPT
  <Description>
  /AUTOSTART_ON=(node1::,node2::) /BASE_PRIORITY=3 /DEFAULT=(FORM=POSTSCRIPT)
  /NOENABLE_GENERIC /OWNER=[grp,mem] /PROCESSOR=TCPWARE_TSSYM
  /PROTECTION=(S:M,O:D,G:M,W:S) /SCHEDULE=(NOSIZE)

$ SHOW LOGICAL/FULL/SYSTEM TCPWARE_TSSYM_QUEUE
  "TCPWARE_TSSYM_QUEUE" [exec] = "ipname,9100,noff"


TCPware LPD:

$ SHOW QUEUE/FULL QUEUE
Server queue queue idle, on node1::, mounted form POSTSCRIPT
  <Description>
  /AUTOSTART_ON=(node1::,node2::) /BASE_PRIORITY=3 /DEFAULT=(FORM=POSTSCRIPT)
  /LIBRARY=library Lowercase /OWNER=[grp,mem] /PROCESSOR=TCPWARE_LPRSMB
  /PROTECTION=(S:M,O:D,G:M,W:S) /SCHEDULE=(NOSIZE)

$ SHOW LOGICAL/FULL/SYSTEM TCPWARE_LPR_queue_PRINTER"

  "TCPWARE_LPR_queue_PRINTER" [exec] = "queuename@ipname"


And so on

