From: tiggerlas@aol.com (Tigger LAS)
Subject: BA23 2nd Hard Drive Modification
Date: 1998/01/08
Message-ID: <19980108184801.NAA16951@ladder01.news.aol.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 314023607
X-Admin: news@aol.com
Organization: AOL http://www.aol.com
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec



Since I received a few requests, I thought I'd post this for anyone interested:


Here's the instructions for modifying the BA23 4-button front-panel,
to force a 2nd hard drive to be "ready" and "write-enabled" full-time.

Remove the front panel from the system.
There are 6 screws you need to take out. They are all plainly visible
from the front of the unit.  Four hold the front panel onto the chassis,
the other two hold the power switch onto the front panel.

Remove the mounting plate from the front panel,
so you can access the solder-side of the board.

Look at the 20-pin connector, from the solder side,
with the connector pointing towards you.

The connector is numbered:

1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15, 17, and 19 on the top row (towards the middle), and
2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 18, and 20 on the bottom (towards the edge).

Connect pins 5 & 6 to +5 volts, using two 560-ohm 1/4 watt resistors.
+5 volts is available at pins 17 & 18 of the 20-pin connector.

I would NOT recommend tying them directly to +5 volts.  Use the resistors!
(If you don't have 560-ohm resistors, I'd imagine that you could use just about
 anything, up to about 1 or 2K. . . .)


Re-install in reverse order. . . .


