Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Digital Equipment
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Check to see if the BIOS setting called PLUG&PLAY is set to YES (if you're
using Win95 - NO if NT). The resource conflict is happening during POST and
the BIOS is senseing that two devices are using the same resources (probably
IRQ). If the SB has jumpers, examine the jumpers to determine what the board
is set for. Then boot the system (without the SB installed) and check what
Win95 indicates your system is using for resources - check in Device Manager
under Computer and click on Properties. Use should then see what resources
are being used. Set your SB card for unused resources.

regards,

glen kelley
digital

