Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Digital Equipment
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


There is a new BIOS update for the Starion 960 on the Digital WEB site. It
might help (it fixes a number of small problems).

In general, the Starion BIOS senses the new card and disables itself.
Windows95 on the other hand, still sees the on-board video.

First, pull the new card and get Windows working properly. Once you are
sure that the video is working correctly, you need to disable (check the
"disable in this hardware profile" box) the S3 video in Device Manager
(don't delete it, Win95 will still find it during boot), set the video to
VGA basic (640x480x256) and then shut down. Now install the new card and
boot up. If you do not see any video from the new card (remember to move
the CRT cable), it may be that the BIOS can not recognize the new card.

regards,

glen kelley
digital

