Why do you need a GUI interface for FTP?
IIS V2.0 comes on the Windows NT CD-ROM as you know and the Windows NT
V4.0 Service Pack 3 contains the stuff to bring it up to IIS V3.0.
FTP is administered through the Internet Information Service Menu located
in STart menu bar/button.

When you apply Service Pack 3, save the OS subdirectory on the small
partition so that you can put the HAL and PAL code back after the Service
Pack is installed. Microsoft unfortunately wipes out the good HAL and PAL
and replaces them with some old stuff.

The message you describe is because you are trying to run 80x86 code on
the Alpha, and this code being very intimate with the OS will not run
properly under the emulator. You may try FX!32, available for free from
DIgital.

