Lee Johnson <johnson@dowell.slb.com> wrote:
: Does anyone know how to change the IP address on a Microvax 3100-40?
: We have 2 on site and need to change the IP address on one of the
: machines and have very little documentation on the machines.

Because TCP/IP isn't incorporated into VMS (assuming these machines
run VMS), you could at least have provided us with the information
_which_ TCP/IP stack you are running.

Assuming DEC TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS (sufficiently recent version),
use

$ @SYS$MANAGER:UCX$CONFIG

or - more directly - the UCX SHOW/SET INTERFACE commands (try UCX HELP
for information on qualifiers and parameters).

