I challenge you to find one of these benchmarks where
Digital has a performance lead.

TPC-C, Third behind Sun and HP if you include clustered
numbers and 4th behind SGI if you
are only interested in single systems.

TPC-D, never published a 1 TB or 300 GB number where the big
boys play. In the 100 GB
tests they are 4th behind NCR, DG and Sun (Sun used a
E450) Digital used an 8400 ouch.

Laddis, Second behind Sun but the product they benchmarked
is not longer marketed, so
6th behind Sun, EMC, Auspex, SGI and HP.

SAP SD, 5th behind Sun, IBM, HP and Sequent.

BaaN, 4th beind HP, Sun and Sequent.

Lotus Notes Bench, Wow Second behind Sun.

SPECweb96, third behind Sun and Fujitsu.

So despite having a clear SPECint95 CPU performance lead
Digital have been unable
to translate this into a "server benchmark" performance
lead.


