The OSF/1 PAL-code interrupt entry at 0x100 produces a stack frame
of PS,PC,GP,A0,A1,A2 before determining the source of the interrupt
and calling ptEntInt.

On my eb164, A0, A1 and A2 seems not to be stacked properly. The
stack slots for these registers contain zero, and the registers
are thus corrupted upon return. It seems only to happen when the
machine is in user mode at the time of the interrupt.

Can anyone help?

