Certainly true - although the part about "an OS that can use it"
is just as important. 128-CPU computers tend to be special-purpose
boxes for scientific computing and other trivially parallel tasks.
(If you have such a task, by all means use an E10000, a Cray/SGI box,
or if the job can be partitioned well enough, a cluster of Linux
workstations).

