That's such a ridiculous, completely untrue statement.  It's no wonder you have no reference for it.  If you want
to compare CPUs, as you seem to, then look at CPU benchmarks such as SPECbench.

Cint95: (#cpus not a factor)
DEC's best   18.0
HP's best    17.3
SUN's best   12.3
SGI's best   11.4
from http://www.specbench.org/osg/cpu95/results/cint95.html

Cfp95: (#cpus a factor)
DEC's best   56.7   8 cpus
HP's best    22.1  16 cpus
SUN's best   34.7  12 cpus
SGI's best   62.5  16 cpus
from http://www.specbench.org/osg/cpu95/results/cfp95.html

Let's end this thread by saying that both systems are enterprise-class players and worthy of a place in most IT
shops.  But you know what?  You can't buy either one of them yet!

Cheers,
