dbond wrote:
> 
> I have a Digital Hinote VP565 notebook.  It advertises that it has a
> large 12.1 inch LCD display.  However, I have a 1 inch blank border
> around the display.  How can I take advantage of the entire display?????

Unlike a CRT, the dot size on a LCD cannot be altered.  When the HiNote
boots, it does so in 640x480 mode.  If you want to take advantage of
your entire screen size, you'll need to increase the resolution under
W95 to at least 800x600.  To do this, right click on a blank area of the
screen, select properties, and settings.  Move the slider to the right,
test your settings, and click OK.  You may have to reboot, but that
should do the trick.

