Dann Lunsford wrote:

> Huh?  Some wierd things in the countdown test line, too.  "A_.." and
> "3_..2_..1?..".  What do those "_" mean?

The underscore thing means "not installed/for future use". "A" and "2" were
never used (far to my knowledge), "3" means the DSH32-S Serial line controller
board. "1" is the Ethernet NI, so you are missing the terminators.

>  Boot VMS. Can't boot VMS, blows up a little after the banner
> prints, screen scrolls way too fast to read.  ANAL/CRASH tells me no valid
> dump.  *sigh*   Try other machine, same thing.  Try other modules,
> *CRASH*, "No valid dump".  Only thing I can think of is a graphics device
> buffer area conflict.

Some early versions of VMS tend to crash after a system upgrade due to
misconfigured SYSGEN files. Try to boot via OPA0:, spawn the
"SYSTARTUP_V5.COM" and then run AUTOGEN. Booting via OPA0:  is found in the
FAQ, so I don't post it here. Try to look at "I FORGOT MY SYSTEM PASSWORD".

Try out: http://www.levitte.org/~ava/vms_faq.htmlx

Regards
Chris





