A small group of Alpha users are already engaged in a different
cryptographic-related challege over at Rob Harley's place.  One thing
that I have learned so far is that a lower level of compiler optimization
may actually increase the speed of the client program.  In particular,
the -O2 gcc option produces faster code than the -O3 option on my
