I just read the Ultrix FAQ (great job), but I did not find anything 
about the maximum SCSI disk size allowed with Ultrix 4.3. I once got
in trouble with Ultrix 4.1, because I did not know about the 1 GB size 
limitation: I got no error message when I did the newfs and mounted a 2GB 
disk, and, after a few days, most on the files on the disk were damaged!

In order to prevent similar problems, I am asking the following question.
Is it possible to use a 4.2 GB disk with Ultrix 4.3? My particular 
situation is as follows: I have installed the 4.2GB disk on an 
ALPHA and I am mounting it, via nfs, from a Decstation 3100 running Ultrix 4.3,
which will perform most of the read/write operations on this disk.

Should I expect any trouble?

Thank you in advance for any reply.

