In article <68j6tv$vkj$1@croci.unipi.it>,
Massimo Macucci <nodump@mercurio.iet.unipi.it> wrote:
>
>I just read the Ultrix FAQ (great job), but I did not find anything 
>about the maximum SCSI disk size allowed with Ultrix 4.3. I once got
>in trouble with Ultrix 4.1, because I did not know about the 1 GB size 
>limitation: I got no error message when I did the newfs and mounted a 2GB 
>disk, and, after a few days, most on the files on the disk were damaged!
>

Ultrix after version 4.2 can suport a partition up to 2GB. 
The disk that the system boots from is limited to 1GB by certain 
processors (some vaxstations , microVAXen, and maybe the ds3100?)
so check which machine youre runing before booting off of a disk > 1gb,
but once the system is up there is no trouble with a 4 gig physical
disk, as long as no partition is bigger than 2 GB. 
Versions of ultrix before 4.2 will barf on partitions bigger than 1 GB.

happy hacking,
isildur



