The problem with this post is that Intel has NOT bought the
Alpha, in any sense. Rather, DEC has gotten use of Intel's
fabrication facilities and unloaded a fab of its own which
it could not fill.

Intel doesn't even have the only Alpha fab; Samsung has another,
and there may be more in the future. However, DEC need not
wait for its own semi process to be debugged now for the next
couple generations of Alpha after EV6. Major speedup for
release of the parts.

The patent cross licensing arguably could work to Intel's
benefit, but just as likely will not, and at any rate the
Alpha design group remains DEC's group, not Intel's.

Thus the premises are wrong...

